    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="Prol.">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:WlEp">Wl ep</ref> Prol.</head>
        <ab type="editionText" xml:lang="la" source="#robertson" n="Prol." corresp="#wit-lp"><pb n="234" ed="#robertson"/>W[illelmus], Dei gratia rex Anglorum, R[adulfo] Bainardo et G[osfrido] de Magnavilla, P[etro] de Valoines ceterisque meis fidelibus de Essex et de Hertfordschire et de Middelsexe—salutem.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#robertson" corresp="#wit-lp"><pb n="235" ed="#robertson"/>William, by the grace of God King of England, to Ralph Bainard and Geoffrey de Maundeville and Peter de Valognes and the rest of my loyal subjects in Essex, Hertfordshire and Middlesex—greeting.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">Added October 2026 from Robertson pp. 234–235 (text and translation); Liebermann’s text (K–M) not yet added</note>
      </div>
    </body>
